pragma hyperion >=0.0.1;

/**
 * Centralised file-level custom errors shared by every Ark Staking contract.
 *
 * File-level errors keep duplicated revert-string data out of the deployed
 * bytecode, which matters more here than on Ethereum: an ML-DSA-87 signature
 * plus public key adds ~7.2KB to every Zond transaction, so creation code above
 * ~18KB can no longer be deployed in a single request.
 *
 * ONLY THE ERRORS THIS PRODUCT ACTUALLY RAISES BELONG HERE. The version this
 * was cut down from carried 25 declarations, 22 of which named insurance
 * conditions (policy status, attestation deadlines, Merkle epochs, Q-Day) that
 * nothing in this repository can reach. Unused declarations cost no bytecode,
 * which is exactly why they accumulate unnoticed — and a shared error file that
 * lists conditions the code cannot produce is a map of a system that is not
 * here. Anything specific to one contract stays in that contract's interface,
 * next to the rule it enforces.
 */

/// A zero address was supplied where a live account or contract is required.
error ZeroAddress();

/// A zero value was supplied where a non-zero amount or identifier is required.
error ZeroValue();

/// A token or native-value transfer returned false or reverted.
error TransferFailed(address recipient, uint256 amount);
